            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Call an electrician to install pendant lights within your ceiling or walls. If you want your mason jar lights to hang directly from the ceiling, you should not try to install them on your own, unless you have extensive experience with electrical wiring. Alternatively, you can string the cord along your wall or ceiling, outside of the wall plaster, and plug it into an electrical outlet.<reF>http://mountainmodernlife.com/25-creative-ways-to-light-up-mason-jars/</ref>[[Image:Make Mason Jar Lights Step 14 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Call an electrician to install pendant lights within your ceiling or walls. If you want your mason jar lights to hang directly from the ceiling, you should not try to install them on your own, unless you have extensive experience with electrical wiring. Alternatively, you can string the cord along your wall or ceiling, outside of the wall plaster, and plug it into an electrical outlet.<reF>http://mountainmodernlife.com/25-creative-ways-to-light-up-mason-jars/</ref>{{expertgreenbox:161062|'''Expert Trick''': For an easy alternative, place some battery-powered fairy lights inside of a mason jar! You can change the color of the light by painting the jar with some translucent paint. You can also try coating the jar with a layer of Mod Podge dyed with food coloring.|}}[[Image:Make Mason Jar Lights Step 14 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
